    <string name="help_median">Your typical %1$s: half of your %2$s are below it, half above. One unusual %1$s doesn\'t move it.</string>
    <string name="help_trimmed_mean">The average after setting aside the highest and lowest 10%% of %2$s, so a few unusual %2$s barely count.</string>
    <string name="help_iqr">How spread out your middle half of %2$s is: from the first quartile (Q1) to the third (Q3), shown under it. A small number means you\'re consistent.</string>
    <string name="help_range">Your lowest and highest %1$s in the window.</string>
    <string name="help_first_entry">The usual time of your first entry of the day (after the day starts). For smoking, a later first cigarette is one of the clearest signs of progress.</string>
    <string name="help_last_entry">The usual time of your last entry of the day.</string>
    <string name="help_since_last">How long it has been since your last entry.</string>
    <string name="help_change">Your last 7 %2$s compared with the 7 before: minus means fewer.</string>
    <string name="help_zero_periods">How many %2$s in the window had no entry at all.</string>
    <string name="help_within_target">How many of your last 30 %2$s stayed at or under your target. One miss doesn\'t reset anything. Set the target in Customize.</string>
    <string name="help_median_gap">The usual time between two entries.</string>
    <string name="help_mean">The plain average. A few heavy %2$s pull it up, so read it next to the median.</string>
    <string name="help_std_dev">How much your %2$s usually differ from the average. Heavy %2$s inflate it, like the mean.</string>
    <string name="help_variance">The square of the standard deviation; for one series it is also its covariance with itself.</string>
    <string name="help_min">Your lowest %1$s in the window.</string>
    <string name="help_max">Your highest %1$s in the window.</string>
    <string name="help_total">Every entry in the window, including the current %1$s.</string>
    <string name="help_count_card">How many entries the selected %1$s has. Use the arrows or the calendar to look at another one.</string>
    <string name="help_stats_card">Statistics of the %2$s in the chart window. The %1$s still running is left out, so a half-finished %1$s doesn\'t count as a low one. Tap a value for what it means, or Customize to change the period or what you see.</string>
    <string name="help_history">One bar per %1$s. A red bar is unusually high (above Q3 + 1.5 × IQR); the solid line is the median and the dashed one the mean. Tap or drag across the bars to look at one.</string>
    <string name="help_time_of_day">How likely you are to do it around each time of day: 100%% means around that time every day.</string>
    <string name="help_positions">The share of each weekday, day of the month or month on which you logged it at least once.</string>
    <string name="help_entries">Every entry of the selected %1$s. Tap + to add one you forgot, or an entry to delete it.</string>
