    <string name="help_mean_typical">The average without the %2$s flagged as unusually high (above Q3 + 1.5 × IQR): what an ordinary %1$s looks like.</string>
    <string name="help_hours">Of all entries in the chart window, the share in each hour of the day. The three busiest hours are darker: that\'s where a nudge or a replacement ritual helps most.</string>
    <string name="help_first_entry_card">The time of your first entry of each day (after the day starts): the median, and the middle half from Q1 to Q3. Research marks the time to the first cigarette after waking as the best single sign of dependence, so a later median is a win.</string>
    <string name="help_weekdays">The median of each weekday, with a line from Q1 to Q3, so one heavy Saturday doesn\'t make every Saturday look heavy. It needs a few weeks of data to be reliable.</string>
    <string name="help_session_trend">Each dot is a session; the line is the median of the last 7 sessions and the dashed line your target. A falling line means you calm down faster.</string>
